# plugin/commands/ — slash commands

Every `.md` file here becomes a slash command namespaced by the plugin name, so
`status.md` is invoked as **`/laika:status`**.

That is why this file has **no `.md` extension**. Named `README.md` it registers
as a junk `/laika:README` command — verified, not assumed: invoking it expanded
`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` and ran through the command pipeline. Unlike `skills/`,
where a loose `.md` is inert, `commands/` scans every `.md` it finds. Do not add
one here that is not meant to be a command.

## Here now

| Command | File | Landed in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/laika:status` | `status.md` | **LAI-012** (M1) |

`/laika:status` is the vertical slice: it proves the manifest, the command
loader, `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}`, and the `scripts/` directory are wired together
correctly. It reads only the environment, never the network, so it works before
any server exists.

## Filled in M4

| Command | Needs | Blocked until |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/laika:setup` | token mint + `npx laika init` | M3 (tokens), M4 (CLI) |
| `/laika:tasks` | MCP `list_ready_tasks` | M3 |
| `/laika:standup` | activity feed for the actor | M3 |

Do not stub these against endpoints that do not exist yet — a command that
always fails is worse than a command that is absent. See SPEC §5 for the
intended behaviour of each.
